runs/EXP_RQ0_5_REPORT.md:217:> "On the BOCoDe development panel, the frozen dimension rule showed an advantage under the selected aggregate. On the held-out IOH/BBOB f1–f5 panel, however, its mean normalized regret was 0.463 versus 0.428 for AlwaysSurrogate (difference +0.036, 95% CI [−0.012, 0.083], p=0.138). Thus, the BOCoDe advantage did not reproduce on this panel, providing no evidence that dimension alone yields a transferable routing benefit."
