    83	| **Hartmann** | 0.670 | 0.785 | **0.473** | **−29.4%** | **−39.7%** |
    84	| Rastrigin | 0.446 | 0.426 | 0.371 | −16.8% | −12.9% |
    85	| Ackley | 0.560 | 0.282 | 0.315 | −43.8% | +11.7% |
    86	
    87	**Interpretation (per codex, revised)**:
    88	- **Hartmann**: RF improves on Surrogate by 29.4%. Wins on 8/10 seeds. **Paired bootstrap CI for Surrogate−RF is [−0.038, 0.415]; two-sided paired t p=0.141.** Publishable as suggestive pilot evidence, not "confirmed."
    89	- **Rastrigin**: RF's gain over fold-specific constant is 0.055, bootstrap CI **[−0.001, 0.120]**. **Conclude "no incremental state signal demonstrated," not "no state information helps."**
    90	- **Ackley**: best fixed action `local_exploitation` (0.282) beats RF (0.315). **RF is no better than the fixed baseline; the −44% vs Surrogate is not state-conditional learnability — it shows Surrogate is the wrong baseline action.**
    95	- 10 seeds + 60-80 records per family is **not sufficient** for definitive learnability claims.
