    97	## 4. Step 3 — Closed-loop terminal regret
    98	
    99	For each (problem, seed), replay trajectory with one first action, then AlwaysSurrogate continuation. 3 seeds × 5 families × 8 first-actions × budget=15.
   100	
   101	| Family | STOP | global_exploration | **local_exploitation** | surrogate_acquisition | boundary_sampling |
   102	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   103	| Branin | 7.32 | 0.52 | — | 0.54 | — |
   104	| Hartmann | 1.16 | 0.52 | **0.33** | 0.48 | 0.53 |
   105	| Ackley | 0.30 | 0.00 | **0.005** | 0.03 | 0.03 |
   106	| SixHumpCamel | 1.90 | 0.31 | — | 0.12 | — |
   107	| Rastrigin | 34.19 | 2.33 | **0.00** | 11.10 | 11.10 |
   108	
   109	(`—` = not in the tested set; only stop / global / surrogate were tested in the smoke run; full 8-action run is in `runs/exp_rq1_3_closed_loop_regret.json`)
   110	
   111	### 4.1 Revised interpretation
   112	
   113	**`local_exploitation` is the best first action on Hartmann, Ackley, and Rastrigin** under AlwaysSurrogate continuation. The earlier "global_exploration wins on Rastrigin" was based on a 3-seed sample that did not test local_exploitation. **The 4.8× ratio I claimed between global and Surrogate is real for that 3-seed subset, but local_exploitation does strictly better.**
   114	
   115	The LLM +8.87 advantage on Rastrigin (EXP-RQ0.5) is therefore more likely attributable to **LLM picking local_exploitation-style actions** than global_exploration. **Without per-step LLM action logs, this remains mechanistic plausibility, not causal validation.** (Per codex round-3 review.)
   116	
   117	## 5. EXP-RQ0.5 — LLM-as-System-1 (status)
   118	
   119	The real-DeepSeek pilot on Rastrigin (2 seeds, budget=20) showed LLM-System-1 beating AlwaysSurrogate by **+8.87 best_y**. The closed-loop regret experiment here is **consistent** with that finding (LLM likely picks the local_exploitation-style actions that win), but **does not validate it** because:
   120	
   121	- EXP-RQ0.5 did not save per-step LLM action logs (token counts all zero)
   122	- The 4.8× ratio in closed-loop was driven by one of three seeds
   123	- Budgets differ (15 here, 20 in EXP-RQ0.5)
   124	
   125	**Status**: suggestive pilot evidence; requires 5-seed replication with per-step LLM action logging before any causal claim. **Deferred.**
